# Engine rules — `src/engine`, `src/worker`, `src/shared`

## Purity (ADR-009) — machine-enforced, non-negotiable

`src/engine/**` may import **only** from `src/engine/**` and `src/shared/types/**`.

It must never reference: `window`, `document`, `navigator`, `localStorage`, `fetch`, `console`,
`process`, `require`, or `performance` (inject a `Clock` instead).

`scripts/check-boundaries.mjs` enforces this in CI. **Never weaken the checker to pass — fix the code.**

Layering matrix: `worker/` → `engine/` + `shared/` · `render/` → `shared/` + theme types ·
`ui/` → `shared/` + `render/types` + `themes/` + `audio/` · `server/` → `shared/` and
`validateRuleSet` from the engine only.

## Multi-state from commit one (ADR-001)

A cell is a `StateId` (unsigned int, `0` = dead), **not a boolean**. Conway is the degenerate
2-state case, not the privileged one. Rules are *data* (`RuleSet` with a state palette, a
neighbourhood and a transition spec), never code branches.

## Grid representation (ADR-010)

Sparse `Map` of dense **32×32 `Uint8Array` chunks**, lazily allocated, pooled and reclaimed.
Each chunk maintains `population`, `perStateCounts`, `dirty`, `lastTick` and a border-occupancy
mask **incrementally** — never recount by scanning. These summaries also feed the statistics
engine and the Phase 5 density LOD: one structure, three consumers.

## Determinism is load-bearing

Same ruleset + seed + boundary mode + edit log ⇒ **bit-identical state at any tick, on any
platform, in any build.** All randomness flows through the injected seedable `Mulberry32`.
Time travel, the Laboratory diff and every test oracle depend on this.

## Hot-loop discipline

- **Zero allocation in steady state.** Preallocate and reuse; `ChangeSet` buffers are reused
  across ticks and callers must not retain them.
- Iterate `activeChunks` only. Fast path over the 30×30 chunk interior with no bounds checks;
  bounds-checked slow path for the border ring.
- No per-cell function calls, no `switch` inside the loop — the rule compiler emits a lookup
  table or a monomorphic closure once, cached by ruleset identity.

## Changes are first-class

`step()` returns a `ChangeSet`. History, statistics and dirty-rect rendering are all derived from
it (ADR-007). Never make it a side effect.

## Correctness bar

Verified against externally-known truths, not just against itself: glider returns translated
(1,1) after 4 generations; R-pentomino stabilises at generation **1103** with **116** cells;
acorn at **5206** / **633**; Gosper gun period 30; toroidal glider returns after 128 generations
on a 32×32 torus.

Coverage gate: **95% statements / 90% branches on `src/engine/**`.** May be raised, never lowered.

## Performance work (Phase 5)

Every fast path — bitboard kernel, chunk skipping, HashLife — must prove **byte-identical
equivalence** against the scalar reference kernel over a large random corpus before it is
accepted. The scalar kernel is never deleted; it is the permanent oracle.
